{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"exact-identities-and-reductions","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:3a21b4e02b3d2d930ab451d425e96d8c6264fdace0f75c4a360ed23d391dbb69/papers/long.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=d70bb160bfefc1577b48160e899f6ed7d8cca34f47089a3f1d1b07c8915075fa","passage_ref":"sha256:d4cff05445a8091e88a0215dc5b8dd28497dfc8c7317357a03f3ed6190b2e19c/papers/long.md/sha256:3a21b4e02b3d2d930ab451d425e96d8c6264fdace0f75c4a360ed23d391dbb69/papers/long.json/passages/exact-identities-and-reductions","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=d70bb160bfefc1577b48160e899f6ed7d8cca34f47089a3f1d1b07c8915075fa&paper=long&passage=exact-identities-and-reductions","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=d70bb160bfefc1577b48160e899f6ed7d8cca34f47089a3f1d1b07c8915075fa&paper=long&passage=exact-identities-and-reductions","span":{"end_byte":190836,"end_line":2055,"start_byte":157177,"start_line":1656},"stage":"long"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=d70bb160bfefc1577b48160e899f6ed7d8cca34f47089a3f1d1b07c8915075fa&view=arguments&node=long.lem-denominator-survival&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=d70bb160bfefc1577b48160e899f6ed7d8cca34f47089a3f1d1b07c8915075fa&node=long.lem-denominator-survival&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=d70bb160bfefc1577b48160e899f6ed7d8cca34f47089a3f1d1b07c8915075fa&node=long.lem-denominator-survival&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=d70bb160bfefc1577b48160e899f6ed7d8cca34f47089a3f1d1b07c8915075fa&view=arguments&node=long.lem-denominator-survival&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=d70bb160bfefc1577b48160e899f6ed7d8cca34f47089a3f1d1b07c8915075fa&ref=sha256%3Af31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5%2Fnodes%2Flong.lem-denominator-survival","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"The evidence mapping records a Lean statement that implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.lem-denominator-survival"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.lem-denominator-survival"],"id":"long.lem-denominator-survival","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Lemma 6.56 (A guaranteed divisor of a reduced denominator)","locator":"Long record Lemma 6.56, p. 59, label lem:denominator-survival","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $a\\in\\mathbb Z$, $D\\in\\mathbb N_{>0}$ and $m,C,h\\in\\mathbb N$. Write $\\operatorname{den}(x)$ for the positive reduced denominator of a rational number $x$. If $m\\mid D$ and $\\gcd(m,|a|)=1$, then $m\\mid\\operatorname{den}(a/D)$. If $C\\mid D$ and $\\gcd(C,|a|)=1$, then\n$$\n\\frac{C}{\\gcd(C,h)}\\mid\\operatorname{den}(ha/D).\n$$\nThus scaling may remove part of the guaranteed divisor. Indeed, reduction divides $D$ by $\\gcd(D,|a|)$, so no prime power in $m$ can be lost. After scaling, a prime $p\\mid C$ can lose at most $v_p(h)$ powers from the guaranteed divisor. This is a lower bound on the reduced denominator, not an equality: for $D=12$, $C=6$, $a=1$, $h=2$, it guarantees the divisor $3$, while the reduced denominator is $6$. The lemma feeds Theorem 6.24 directly.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.lem-denominator-survival","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.lem-denominator-survival","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.lem-denominator-survival%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.RationalDenominatorSurvival.divisor_dvd_divInt_den%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.lem-denominator-survival%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.RationalDenominatorSurvival.divisor_dvd_divInt